stic equals the Betti number",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>Lefschetz trace formula</strong>: |X(𝔽_{q^k})| = Σ_{i} (−1)^i Tr(Fr^k | H^i_{ét}(X, ℚ_ℓ)), generalizing the classical Lefschetz fixed-point formula."},{id:43502,text:"🔥 The Fontaine-Mazur conjecture characterizes:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"Geometric Galois representations — those arising from étale cohomology",c:true},{l:"B",t:"All Galois representations of finite image",c:false},{l:"C",t:"The maximal abelian extension of ℚ",c:false},{l:"D",t:"The structure of the absolute Galois group",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>Fontaine-Mazur conjecture</strong>: an ℓ-adic Galois representation is geometric (comes from a smooth projective variety) iff it is unramified outside finitely many primes and potentially semistable at ℓ."},{id:43503,text:"🔥 The modularity theorem (Wiles et al.) states:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"Every elliptic curve over ℚ is modular — its L-function matches a weight-2 modular form",c:true},{l:"B",t:"Every elliptic curve over ℚ has complex multiplication",c:false},{l:"C",t:"Modular forms are always cusp forms",c:false},{l:"D",t:"All Galois representations are modular",c:false}],sol:"The <strong>modularity theorem</strong> (Wiles, Breuil-Conrad-Diamond-Taylor): every elliptic curve over ℚ is associated to a modular form of weight 2, level N, and trivial character."},{id:43504,text:"🔥 Fermat's Last Theorem follows from:",opts:[{l:"A",t:"The modularity of the Frey curve + Ribet's level-lowering theorem",c:true},{l:"B",t:"The Weil conjectures alone",c:false},{l:"C",t:"The Mordell-Weil theorem",c:false},{l:"D",t:"The Hodge conjecture",c:false}],sol:"<strong>Fermat's Last Theorem</strong>: if aⁿ + bⁿ = cⁿ, the Frey curve E: y² = x(x−aⁿ)(x+bⁿ) would be modular (by the modularity theorem) yet Ribet's theorem shows its level cannot be lowered to 2 — a contradiction, hence no such solution exists."}];
